WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.186
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level two.

2
00:00:06.486 --> 00:00:09.965
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.265 --> 00:00:16.586
Unit one: Stock Market Basics. Today you will discuss hypothetical investing with the second conditional.

4
00:00:16.886 --> 00:00:19.620
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:23.927
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:25.657
Stock.

7
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.544
Stock means a share of ownership in a company.

8
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.848
She bought stock in a local bank.

9
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.789
Your turn. Say: Stock.

10
00:00:37.633 --> 00:00:38.437
Stock.

11
00:00:39.183 --> 00:00:40.057
Share.

12
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:43.340
Share means one unit of a company's stock.

13
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.135
Each share rose by two dollars.

14
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.926
Your turn. Say: Share.

15
00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:52.686
Share.

16
00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:54.567
Investor.

17
00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:59.069
Investor means a person who puts money into something to make a profit.

18
00:00:59.683 --> 00:01:02.066
The investor studied the company's accounts.

19
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.186
Your turn. Say: Investor.

20
00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:09.162
Investor.

21
00:01:09.917 --> 00:01:11.220
Market index.

22
00:01:12.217 --> 00:01:16.202
Market index means a number showing how a group of stocks is performing.

23
00:01:16.817 --> 00:01:19.908
The market index closed higher on Friday.

24
00:01:20.517 --> 00:01:23.517
Your turn. Say: Market index.

25
00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:27.600
Market index.

26
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.432
Bull market.

27
00:01:30.417 --> 00:01:33.833
Bull market means a period when stock prices keep rising.

28
00:01:34.417 --> 00:01:37.090
A bull market encourages new investors.

29
00:01:37.683 --> 00:01:40.510
Your turn. Say: Bull market.

30
00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:44.542
Bull market.

31
00:01:45.283 --> 00:01:46.296
Bear market.

32
00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:50.595
Bear market means a period when stock prices keep falling.

33
00:01:51.183 --> 00:01:53.624
Many investors panic in a bear market.

34
00:01:54.217 --> 00:01:56.614
Your turn. Say: Bear market.

35
00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:00.561
Bear market.

36
00:02:01.317 --> 00:02:02.213
Dividend.

37
00:02:03.217 --> 00:02:06.342
Dividend means a payment a company makes to its shareholders.

38
00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:09.356
The firm paid a dividend of fifty cents.

39
00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:12.800
Your turn. Say: Dividend.

40
00:02:15.633 --> 00:02:16.530
Dividend.

41
00:02:17.283 --> 00:02:18.377
Portfolio.

42
00:02:19.383 --> 00:02:23.206
Portfolio means all the investments that a person or fund owns.

43
00:02:23.817 --> 00:02:26.501
A balanced portfolio spreads the risk.

44
00:02:27.117 --> 00:02:29.537
Your turn. Say: Portfolio.

45
00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.540
Portfolio.

46
00:02:34.333 --> 00:02:37.787
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.996
Visal, if you had a thousand dollars, would you buy stock?

48
00:02:43.083 --> 00:02:52.272
I would, but only if I understood the risk. If I owned a diverse portfolio, a fall in one share would not hurt me badly.

49
00:02:53.383 --> 00:02:55.069
What would you watch in the news?

50
00:02:56.183 --> 00:03:03.805
I would follow the market index. If it kept rising, we would call it a bull market; if it kept falling, a bear market.

51
00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:06.556
And would a dividend matter?

52
00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:15.643
Yes. If a company paid a steady dividend, an investor could earn income even when the share price stayed flat.

53
00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.312
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:23.936
Grammar focus: Second conditional: hypothetical situations.

55
00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:25.434
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:31.087
If I owned a diverse portfolio, I would worry less about one falling share.

57
00:03:31.983 --> 00:03:35.016
If the index kept rising, we would call it a bull market.

58
00:03:35.917 --> 00:03:39.727
If a firm paid a dividend, investors could earn steady income.

59
00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:50.192
Use if + past simple, would + verb for unreal or unlikely situations. In formal writing, use 'were' for all persons: If I were an investor...

60
00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:54.705
Be careful! Don't say: If I would own stock, I would win.

61
00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:58.991
Say: If I owned stock, I would win.

62
00:03:59.291 --> 00:04:00.861
No 'would' in the if-clause.

63
00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:04.284
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.635
Thinking Like an Investor.

65
00:04:06.935 --> 00:04:11.559
Financial news is full of numbers, but each number tells a story about confidence.

66
00:04:12.567 --> 00:04:18.316
A market index measures how a group of stocks is performing, and a rising index signals a bull market.

67
00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:23.250
If prices kept falling for months, analysts would describe a bear market.

68
00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:31.108
An investor who owned a diverse portfolio would be protected, because a dividend from one company could offset a loss from another.

69
00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:36.178
Wise investors would therefore study risk before they buy a single share.

70
00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:41.326
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:42.183 --> 00:04:45.553
If I blank a diverse portfolio, I would worry less.

72
00:04:45.853 --> 00:04:48.926
A, owned. B, own. C, will own.

73
00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:54.919
The answer is A: owned.

74
00:04:56.083 --> 00:04:59.441
A payment a company makes to its shareholders is a blank.

75
00:04:59.741 --> 00:05:03.952
A, dividend. B, portfolio. C, stock index.

76
00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.395
The answer is A: dividend.

77
00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:14.372
A period when stock prices keep falling is a blank market.

78
00:05:14.672 --> 00:05:17.652
A, bull. B, bear. C, share.

79
00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.165
The answer is B: bear.

80
00:05:24.317 --> 00:05:26.096
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:26.396 --> 00:05:33.416
A, If I would own stock, I would win.. B, If I owned stock, I would benefit.. C, If I owned stock, I will benefit..

82
00:05:36.967 --> 00:05:40.638
The answer is B: If I owned stock, I would benefit..

83
00:05:41.783 --> 00:05:45.710
According to the reading, wise investors study blank before buying.

84
00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:49.931
A, risk. B, headlines. C, dividends only.

85
00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:55.466
The answer is A: risk.

86
00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:59.760
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:00.617 --> 00:06:03.731
Why might someone choose to invest in the stock market?

88
00:06:12.517 --> 00:06:13.878
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:14.178 --> 00:06:37.940
Someone might invest in the stock market to grow their savings faster than a bank account would. Over many years, share prices and dividends have often produced higher returns than interest. However, stocks carry risk, so a sensible investor would build a diverse portfolio and invest only money they could leave untouched for a long time.

90
00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.077
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:40.983 --> 00:06:46.329
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and second conditional: hypothetical situations.

92
00:06:46.629 --> 00:06:51.766
Today's value is financial literacy. Understand money well enough to make wise decisions.

93
00:06:52.066 --> 00:06:54.312
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:54.612 --> 00:06:57.439
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

